{{also|Schildern}}
==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃɪldɐn/}}
* {{audio|de|De-schildern.ogg|Audio}}

===Etymology 1===
17th century, from {{bor|de|nl|schilderen|t=to paint, picture}}, in part through {{der|de|gml|schildern}}. Derived from the cognate of {{m|de|Schild|t=shield; sign}}, from the painting of coats of arms on shields and similar objects. Analysable as {{suffix|de|Schild|-ern}}.

====Verb====
{{de-verb}}

# {{lb|de|transitive}} to [[depict]] (with words), to [[narrate]], [[tell]] [[vividly]]
#: {{syn|de|beschreiben|darstellen}}
#: {{ux|de|Der Autor '''schildert''' die Erlebnisse seines Helden in bunten Farben.|t=The author '''depicts''' his hero’s adventures in vivid colours.}}
# {{lb|de|transitive|archaic}} to [[depict]] (by illustration), to [[paint]], [[draw]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{de-conj}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{affix|de|Schild|t1=shield|-ern|pos2=iterative suffix}}. Thus the same as etymology 1, but formed directly, not borrowed.

====Verb====
{{de-verb}}

# {{lb|de|hunting|of [[partridge]]s etc.}} to be in full [[feather]] and have a characteristic [[spot]] on the breast
# {{lb|de|obsolete}} to stand [[guard]], to [[patrol]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{de-conj}}

